# 低频词汇 List02
# 领域: 考研
# 学科: 英语词汇
# 来源: 2024恋练有词
# 描述: 低频词汇List02核心词汇

{{appliance}}{/əˈplaɪəns/}{器具；家用电器}{Modern appliances make household chores much easier.}}
{{appreciation}}{/əˌpriːʃiˈeɪʃn/}{欣赏；感激；增值}{The event was held in appreciation of the volunteers' efforts.}}
{{arbitrary}}{/ˈɑːbɪtrəri/}{任意的；武断的}{The selection process seemed arbitrary and unfair.}}
{{architect}}{/ˈɑːkɪtekt/}{建筑师；设计师}{The architect drew up plans for the new library.}}
{{arise}}{/əˈraɪz/}{出现；产生}{New opportunities may arise from unexpected circumstances.}}
{{artificial}}{/ˌɑːtɪˈfɪʃl/}{人工的；人造的}{Artificial intelligence is reshaping the job market.}}
{{aspire}}{/əˈspaɪər/}{渴望；追求}{Young people aspire to make a difference in the world.}}
{{assault}}{/əˈsɔːlt/}{攻击；袭击}{The assault on democratic institutions was widely criticized.}}
{{asset}}{/ˈæset/}{资产；有用的东西}{Good communication skills are a valuable career asset.}}
{{assimilate}}{/əˈsɪmɪleɪt/}{同化；吸收}{Immigrants often face challenges in assimilating into a new culture.}}
{{astonish}}{/əˈstɒnɪʃ/}{使惊讶}{The magician's performance astonished the audience.}}
{{astronomy}}{/əˈstrɒnəmi/}{天文学}{Astronomy has advanced dramatically with modern telescopes.}}
{{athlete}}{/ˈæθliːt/}{运动员}{The athlete trained for years to compete at the Olympics.}}
{{atrocity}}{/əˈtrɒsəti/}{暴行；残忍}{The atrocities committed during the war shocked the world.}}
{{attendance}}{/əˈtendəns/}{出席；到场}{Attendance at the workshop exceeded all expectations.}}
{{auction}}{/ˈɔːkʃn/}{拍卖}{The rare painting sold for a record price at auction.}}
{{audience}}{/ˈɔːdiəns/}{观众；听众}{The speaker captivated the audience with her story.}}
{{authorize}}{/ˈɔːθəraɪz/}{授权；批准}{Only senior management can authorize such expenditures.}}
{{autonomy}}{/ɔːˈtɒnəmi/}{自治；自主权}{The university values its academic autonomy.}}
{{aviation}}{/ˌeɪviˈeɪʃn/}{航空；飞行}{The aviation industry is investing in sustainable fuels.}}
{{awkward}}{/ˈɔːkwəd/}{尴尬的；笨拙的}{There was an awkward silence during the meeting.}}
{{backbone}}{/ˈbækbəʊn/}{脊柱；支柱}{Agriculture is the backbone of the rural economy.}}
{{badge}}{/bædʒ/}{徽章；标记}{The officer wore a shiny badge on his uniform.}}
{{bail}}{/beɪl/}{保释；保释金}{The suspect was released on $50,000 bail.}}
{{ballot}}{/ˈbælət/}{选票；投票}{Citizens cast their ballots in the national referendum.}}
{{ban}}{/bæn/}{禁止；禁令}{The city imposed a ban on single-use plastics.}}
{{bankruptcy}}{/ˈbæŋkrʌptsɪ/}{破产}{The airline filed for bankruptcy after the pandemic.}}
{{barren}}{/ˈbærən/}{贫瘠的；不育的}{The barren soil made farming nearly impossible.}}
{{batch}}{/bætʃ/}{一批；一组}{The factory produced a fresh batch of vaccines.}}
{{beam}}{/biːm/}{光束；梁；微笑}{She beamed with pride as her son received the award.}}
